.TH KLVTOOL-PACKETIZE 1 "1970-01-01" "klvtool dev" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
klvtool\-packetize \- Replay raw extraction checkpoints into KLV packet checkpoints with framing diagnostics.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
klvtool packetize \-\-input <raw\-checkpoint\-dir> \-\-out <dir> [\-\-mode strict|best\-effort] [\-\-view auto|pretty|raw]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Replay the raw extraction checkpoints produced by `klvtool extract`, parse them into individual KLV packets (key, BER length, value), and write per\-record packet checkpoints under <out> plus a packet manifest summarizing parser counts and diagnostics.
.PP
Use \-\-mode=strict (default) when input is expected to be well\-formed: a malformed packet aborts the record. Use \-\-mode=best\-effort for forensic recovery on suspect or corrupt input — the parser scans forward past malformed packets, recovers what it can, and surfaces diagnostics with byte offsets so an analyst can see exactly where the wire format diverged.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR
raw checkpoint directory produced by `klvtool extract`
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI(default strict)\fR
parser mode: strict or best\-effort
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR
output directory for packet checkpoints
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fI(default auto)\fR
presentation mode: auto, pretty, or raw
.SH "OUTPUT FORMAT"
Each invocation writes per\-record JSON checkpoints under <out>/ plus <out>/packet\-manifest.ndjson with one PacketManifest line per replay.
.SS Fields
.TP
\fBschemaVersion\fR (string)
manifest envelope version
.TP
\fBsourcePath\fR (string)
the \-\-input directory as provided
.TP
\fBrecords[].recordId\fR (string)
matches the recordId from the extract manifest
.TP
\fBrecords[].mode\fR (string)
"strict" or "best\-effort"
.TP
\fBrecords[].parserVersion\fR (string)
klvtool packetizer version that produced the output
.TP
\fBrecords[].parsedCount\fR (integer)
number of well\-formed KLV packets recovered
.TP
\fBrecords[].warningCount\fR (integer)
.TP
\fBrecords[].errorCount\fR (integer)
.TP
\fBrecords[].recovered\fR (boolean)
true if best\-effort recovery skipped past at least one malformed region
.TP
\fBrecords[].packetPath\fR (string)
relative path to the per\-record PacketCheckpoint file
.TP
\fBrecords[].diagnostics\fR (array)
{severity, code, message, stage, packetIndex?, byteOffset?}
.SS Schema stability
Schema is stable within klvtool 1.x: new fields are additive.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Strict packetize after a clean extract
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool packetize --input ./mission-extract --out ./mission-packets
.fi
.RE
.PP
Best\-effort packetize for forensic recovery on corrupt input
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool packetize --input ./mission-extract --out ./mission-packets --mode best-effort
.fi
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
success
.TP
\fB1\fR
input read failure, output write failure, or strict\-mode parse error
.TP
\fB2\fR
invalid usage (including \-\-input and \-\-out pointing at the same directory)
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
disable ANSI color in pretty output
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fB<out>/packet\-manifest.ndjson\fR
summary manifest, one record per source raw checkpoint
.TP
\fB<out>/<recordId>.json\fR
PacketCheckpoint JSON with parsed packets and diagnostics
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBklvtool\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-extract\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-decode\fR(1)
